Task 2: Set Up Dynamic Inventory Using External Cloud Provider
Subtask 2.1: Understanding Dynamic Inventories
Dynamic inventories automatically discover and organize hosts from external sources like cloud providers, databases, or APIs. This eliminates the need to manually maintain static inventory files.

Benefits of Dynamic Inventories:

Automatically updated as infrastructure changes
Reduces manual maintenance overhead
Integrates with cloud provider metadata
Supports auto-scaling environments
