Common Troubleshooting Issues
Issue 1: YAML Syntax Errors
Problem: Inventory file fails to parse due to YAML syntax errors.

Solution:

# Validate YAML syntax
python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('advanced-static-inventory.yml'))"

# Use ansible-inventory to check parsing
ansible-inventory -i advanced-static-inventory.yml --list --yaml
Issue 2: SSH Connection Failures
Problem: Cannot connect to managed hosts.

Solution:

# Test SSH connectivity manually
ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa ansible@192.168.1.10

# Check SSH key permissions
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_rsa

# Add SSH debugging to ansible.cfg
[ssh_connection]
ssh_args = -vvv -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=60s
Issue 3: Dynamic Inventory Not Working
Problem: AWS dynamic inventory returns empty results.

Solution:

# Check AWS credentials
aws sts get-caller-identity

# Test boto3 connection
python3 -c "import boto3; print(boto3.client('ec2').describe_instances())"

# Enable debug mode
./aws_ec2_inventory.py --list 2>&1 | head -20
Issue 4: Variable Precedence Issues
Problem: Variables not applying as expected.

Solution:

# Check variable precedence
ansible-inventory -i advanced-static-inventory.yml --host web1 | jq .

# Test variable resolution in playbook
ansible -i advanced-static-inventory.yml web1 -m debug -a "var=hostvars[inventory_hostname]"
